WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.750
Node.

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:05.046
js application security combines secure coding, dependency governance, runtime validation,

00:00:05.046 --> 00:00:09.771
access control, secrets management, safe file and process handling, careful logging,

00:00:09.771 --> 00:00:11.489
and secure deployment practices.

00:00:11.489 --> 00:00:14.067
The platform is flexible and productive,

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:19.651
but that flexibility means teams must be explicit about trust boundaries, runtime behavior,

00:00:19.651 --> 00:00:20.940
and operational controls.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:21.799
Strong Node.

00:00:21.799 --> 00:00:24.806
js security treats every boundary as untrusted.

00:00:24.806 --> 00:00:28.243
Requests, headers, cookies, files, environment configuration, package scripts,

00:00:28.243 --> 00:00:33.398
third-party APIs, queue messages, logs, and deployment settings can all affect security.

00:00:33.398 --> 00:00:36.834
The application should validate data before business logic,

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:39.841
enforce authorization on the server, limit privileges,

00:00:39.841 --> 00:00:43.707
and fail in ways that are safe and observable.

00:00:43.707 --> 00:00:46.714
Every dependency is a supply chain decision.

00:00:46.714 --> 00:00:51.440
Teams should understand direct and transitive dependencies, maintain lockfiles, review updates,

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.595
use software composition analysis, and prefer packages that are maintained and necessary.

00:00:56.595 --> 00:00:59.602
The point is not to fear npm.

00:00:59.602 --> 00:01:06.045
The point is to make dependency choices visible enough that speed does not erase accountability.

00:01:06.045 --> 00:01:09.482
The goal is not to memorize every vulnerability.

00:01:09.482 --> 00:01:12.059
The goal is to build Node.

00:01:12.059 --> 00:01:15.496
js applications that are explicit, least-privileged, observable, resilient,

00:01:15.496 --> 00:01:17.214
and safe to operate.

00:01:17.214 --> 00:01:22.799
When developers and operators share that mindset, security becomes part of normal engineering:

00:01:22.799 --> 00:01:26.235
clear contracts, careful defaults, reliable deployment, useful monitoring,

00:01:26.235 --> 00:01:30.740
and defensive handling of the data and services the application touches.
